## 12. Communication in Distributed Systems

Nodes need to communicate with each other to exchange information.

Common communication methods:

### 12.1 HTTP/HTTPS

Used for communication between web services and APIs.

### 12.2 RPC (Remote Procedure Call)

Allows one machine to call a function or procedure on another machine.

### 12.3 Message Queues

Allow applications to exchange messages asynchronously.

Examples:
- Apache Kafka
- RabbitMQ

### 12.4 TCP/IP

Provides network communication between computers.

