## 19. Distributed Architecture vs Centralized Architecture

| Centralized Architecture | Distributed Architecture |
|---|---|
| Main processing happens on a central system | Processing happens across multiple nodes |
| Limited scalability | Supports horizontal scaling |
| Central failure can affect the whole service | Can tolerate some node failures |
| Simpler to manage initially | More complex to manage |
| Example: Single-server application | Example: Hadoop cluster |

